1b:T940,-----BEGIN PGP SIGNED MESSAGE-----
Hash: SHA512

diyhrt.coffee — warrant canary
date: 2026-10-21

as of today, diyhrt.coffee:

  1. has not received any government subpoena, search warrant,
     court order, national security letter, or any other
     compelled-disclosure demand for user data, logs, or access.
  2. has not been served any gag order or other form of
     compelled silence.
  3. has not been compromised, coerced, or accessed by any
     party other than its stated operators.
  4. retains full control of its signing keys, infrastructure,
     and source code.

key change: from this canary on, a canary is valid when it is
signed by either of the site's two admins, phi or n2x:

  phi  <admin@diyhrt.coffee>
       493B B8AF 3865 2ADE 4054  D14A B01E E3EB 9676 EFD9
  n2x
       268D 6AE8 A3AA 82BE F3B3  9BE6 97E6 511B BB1F 12CF

this one is signed twice: by phi's new key, and by akira's key,
which signed the canaries before the handover and vouches for it:

  akira
       33AA 9E20 C6D5 FA57 B056  C488 E608 EDED D5FB 9ECF

akira's key is retired after this and won't sign future canaries.
all three keys are published at https://diyhrt.coffee/canary

this canary will be reposted at least once every 30 days. if a
future canary fails to appear when due, isn't signed by one of the
admin keys above, or if any of the four statements above can no
longer be made truthfully, you should assume diyhrt.coffee may
have been compromised.

proof of liveness (these change constantly, so a re-posted old
canary won't match):

  - bitcoin block 972494, mined 2026-10-21 15:39 utc:
    000000000000000000018912d1083009ef298e17cea99e53d2509b7aaaa1111c
  - "US citizen Stephen Hubbard freed by Russia as Trump envoy
    meets Putin" (bbc news, 2026-10-21)
  - "Elon Musk confirms he is considering merging Tesla and
    SpaceX" (bbc news, 2026-10-21)

next canary due: 2026-11-20

— phi
